{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/946274-safe-house","id":946274,"title":"Safe house","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-08T10:36:59-07:00","id":946274,"title":"Safe house","content":"This is something that is causing a bit of debate in our game.<br /> <br /> The safe house merit has specific rules for what the points do which is -1 to -5 to break in a couple of questions about this. One player has said that he will buy safe house and have wiring in the doors that is impossible to see so if someone opens his doors or windows or walls the wire will send a wireless signal to him so he knows he is being infiltrated, which I dont think you should be able to do at all.<br /> <br /> Also he states that from previous threads if an NPC decides to break in they get -5 and follow the safe house rules but if its a player you can set what is there like the impossible to see trip wire so he always knows your breaking in and can add on more stuff to give an even bigger penalty then -5. Or if he gets a lookout in the base then you have to roll to sneak past the look out and then roll to break in.<br /> <br /> He is also stating that safe house rules are for NPC's breaking in not players and if a player dominated/persuaded an NPC to break into their house then they are treated as the player trying to break in so you dont use the -5 rule and you use whatever you've built for the NPC to break in.<br /> <br /> In Summary NPC's breaking in get -5 if a PC breaks in he has to get past everything you've made up to put in there including stuff that no one can ever get past apparently, and if a PC convinces an NPC to break in then you used the rules for PC's breaking in.<br /> <br /> I thought no matter what it is -5 to everyone and the merit includes stuff like look outs and doors with trip wires that you can't see etc.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12176-theboydante","name":"TheBoyDante","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T10:53:04-07:00","id":946281,"title":"","content":"Safe house for players is an abstraction. They have traps and it inflicts the -5 penalty. If the intruder thinks to look for and disable those wires, its a dex + larceny -(Safe Place) roll.<br /> <br /> If the players would like additional security they can buy staff and retainer.<br /> <br /> There is also i think surveilance equipment or cameras or something... its under equipment and gives rules for setting up things like that. You can reskin it to he wires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 08-08-2016, 01:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T11:38:41-07:00","id":946323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBoyDante</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/946274-safe-house#post946274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The safe house merit has specific rules for what the points do which is -1 to -5 to break in a couple of questions about this. One player has said that he will buy safe house and have wiring in the doors that is impossible to see so if someone opens his doors or windows or walls the wire will send a wireless signal to him so he knows he is being infiltrated, which I dont think you should be able to do at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well trying to disguise security features is part of the Safe House Merit effects. A wi-fi text is pretty standard with modern security systems if someone fails to override them as they break in.<br /> <br /> The thing to remember is that if you're not trying to just brute force a physical lock, overcoming security is an extended roll. Player effort/Resources for better security goes into increasing the successes need to bypass security (which is penalized by Safe House), so this:<br /> <br /> [quote]Also he states that from previous threads if an NPC decides to break in they get -5 and follow the safe house rules but if its a player you can set what is there like the impossible to see trip wire so he always knows your breaking in and can add on more stuff to give an even bigger penalty then -5.{/quote]<br /> <br /> Is wrong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or if he gets a lookout in the base then you have to roll to sneak past the look out and then roll to break in. </div> </div> </div>Yep, friendly NPC guards get to guard the Safe House and have to be dealt with by people breaking in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> He is also stating that safe house rules are for NPC's breaking in not players and if a player dominated/persuaded an NPC to break into their house then they are treated as the player trying to break in so you dont use the -5 rule and you use whatever you've built for the NPC to break in. </div> </div> </div>He's wrong. There's no PC/NPC divide in the mechanics (its something the CofD generally avoids).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I thought no matter what it is -5 to everyone and the merit includes stuff like look outs and doors with trip wires that you can't see etc. </div> </div> </div>You're more right, though as noted you can do things to make your Safe House more safe with other systems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T15:40:23-07:00","id":946520,"title":"","content":"This sounds like you've got a player trying to game the system and not playing in good faith. This problem is not going to be resolved by a rules call, as it's merely a symptom of an underlying issue of players and storyteller(s) with different expectations of the buy-in and social contract of this game. You need to have a talk about player and ST expectations and responsibilities, and remind everyone that RPGs are a group activity, and everyone at the table needs to be contributing to making the activity enjoyable for everyone else in the group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T03:24:49-07:00","id":946839,"title":"","content":"The logic was more as follows; <br /> <br /> Player A spends 5 merit dots. Gets a safe house. Goes off and does a jolly adventure, networking, killing things, other general things his character would do.<br /> <br /> Player B gets a safe house. Player B is paranoid and spends all of his in game time as a character tracking down and finding the best lookout in the country. Researching the best defence and protection. Using the crafting rules to create extra traps and fail safes. Basically turning his house into a veritable fort knox by using his time and resources. <br /> <br /> Dantes view is that no matter what you do its -5 no matter what. My view is that if a player spends their time and effort within the game world to accomplish something then it should be reflected in someway to actually create some player agency rather than just 'I spend 5 merit points job done.' <br /> <br /> (And to clarify the rest rose said in a previous post that if an NPC attempts to break into a PC safe house you use the -5, if a PC wants to break into an NPCS you can use the item creation rules to generate a layout for players to bypass. My opinion is that wasn't taking into account player vs player actions and so therefore a player who spends their time hand building their defences shouldn't allow a second player to go &quot;oh well I can't break in, but I hire an NPC and then poof I can ignore all that because it isn't me doing it&quot; and is why we have been butting heads on this topic (all in good faith we often debate rules it makes for good fun) but that is where the NPC/PC divide has come from.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11995-wunderkid","name":"Wunderkid","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T12:18:19-07:00","id":947153,"title":"","content":"I think there's a major problem that's not even mechanical there then. Player A and Player B are, first and foremost, operating under differing playstyles. Some people just like having dots on their sheet and handwaving the rest, others like to go into way more detail about what those dots mean and where they came from.<br /> <br /> Playstyle shouldn't change the mechanical benefits of a Merit. Safehouse provides the same bonuses to the owner(s) regardless of playstyle.<br /> <br /> If the difference is investment, then there's remedies in the system because there are other options you can stack on your Safehouse. But this means mechanical investment as well as RP investment. If you want a guard that does more than justify what your Safehouse is at 5 dots, it should come with the cost of a Retainer that has a dicepool to guard it as set by that Merit. If you have a 5 dot Safehouse guarded by a 5 dot Retainer, then you should get the benefit of both (esp. if you're opting to have a high level Retainer that just sits around and watches your house).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T13:13:40-07:00","id":947188,"title":"","content":"Player B has Safehouse and retainer and the camera/surveillance system equipment. You can already have extra traps, IIRC. No matter what they each deal (Safe House) Lethal Damage or less (unless banes are involved).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}